  "strategy": "We propose a multi-objective optimization strategy using two distinct approaches:\n1) Frequency-domain spectral shaping\n2) Real-space evolution with resampling\n\nKey innovations:\n- Blends gradient-based and evolutionary search\n- Uses cross-domain information transfer (frequency to real-space and vice versa)\n- Automatically adjusts sequence length based on optimization trajectory\n- Implements dynamic time allocation between gradient steps and evolutionary exploration\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize with either parent sequence (if available) or random pattern\n2. Adaptive length management: grow sequence gradually while improving\n3. Two-phase optimization:\n   a) Component-wise spectral correction using gradient descent\n   b) Population-based optimization using crossover and mutation\n4. Bi-directional information exchange between phases\n\nComplexity and Scheduling:\n- Start with base_length=1200 (if parent not given)\n- Progressively increase length if not normalized by previous methods\n- Allocate 30% total time to initial gradient optimization\n- Use remaining time 70% for population search\n\nImplementation Steps:\n\n1. Initialization phase:\n   - If parent is available, use normalized sample. Otherwise random initialization\n   - Compute preliminary score using evaluate_safe\n\n2. Component mapping phase:\n   - Decompose sequence into components based on max autocorrelation peaks\n   - Compute frequency signature of each component (full convolution)\n\n3. Spectrum-adapted optimization:\n   - Use spectral balancing to define hyperparameters\n   - Initialize real-space positions based on frequency strength\n\n4. Evolutionary refinement:\n   - Maintain trial population (3-5 sequences at current length)\n   - Select parental candidates by crossover factor\n   - Apply mutation based on observed spectral inefficiencies\n   - Evaluate and advance best performers with new lengths\n\nFallback handling:\n   - If any child sequence invalid, repair using softmax function\n   - Maintain minimal valid candidate throughout optimization\n   - Normalize if necessary before evaluation\n\n(helper functions)\n\ndef adaptive_spectral_control(a, alpha=0.4):\n    \"\"\"Shapes spectrum towards minimal infinite norm.\"\"\"\n    # (... Code for spectral shaping)\n\ndef evolutionary_adaptation(a, parent_strength, seed=42):\n    \"\"\"Recombines with parent using crossover.\"\"\"\n    # (... Code)\n\ndef main_optimization_loop(base_candidate, iterations=20):\n    \"\"\"Combines both techniques progressively.\"\"\"\n    # (... Code)\n\nFinal fallback: \n   - If any candidate invalid during evolution, use carefully normalized interpolation\n   - Recompute score from scratch to ensure validity\n   - Print final sequence and score for debugging\n\nTime management:\n   - Monitor elapsed time constantly\n   - Scale optimization steps dynamically\n   - Extended parent strategy until score improvement stalls\n\nWe load parent sequence if available, otherwise proceed with randomly initialized patterns.\n\nThis strategy targets improved generalization beyond local optima by leveraging both gradient and stochastic optimization, with length dedication reducing premature stagnation.\n\nIt incrementally adjusts length boundaries ensuring consistent dB improvement while the spectral control stays in control of the shape.\n\nThe interplay is designed to systematically break the problem's symmetries.",
